WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.900
- So Devin Nunes is back in the news.

00:00:01.900 --> 00:00:04.230
We learned that in the waning
days of the Trump presidency,

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:06.190
the Department of
Justice, led by Bill Barr,

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:10.120
issued a subpoena against
Twitter to unmask the identity

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:11.190
of the person that was running

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:14.140
a parody Devin Nunes
account called NunezAlt.

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:16.090
Now, the Department of Justice
said that this was related

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:19.380
to prosecuting potential
threats against the congressmen.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:20.840
Whereas Twitter pushed back.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:22.910
They filed a motion to quash
to prevent the subpoena

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.280
from going forward and
asked for verification

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:26.430
of these supposed threats,

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:27.800
which the Department of Justice apparently

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.910
was not able to provide.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:29.980
It's good that Twitter pushed back

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:32.720
because this was clearly protected
First Amendment activity,

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.380
and apparently the Department of Justice

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.400
dropped the subpoena
after Biden was elected.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:38.720
So we're not gonna see Twitter in court,

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:41.420
but hopefully we'll see
some penalties for the AUSA

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:44.370
that actually filed this subpoena
because this is nonsense.

